---- MODULE MCSpace ----
(***************************************************************************)
(* Small models of Space, with two cells and one read.                     *)
(*                                                                         *)
(* The boids. MCSpace.cfg checks the space as the library makes it, with   *)
(* two boids that write one time each. MCSpaceLong.cfg has one boid that   *)
(* writes three times. The fault models must fail: MCSpaceGap.cfg (a       *)
(* write removes the old copy before it adds the new copy, so a reader     *)
(* does not find a boid that stays in its cell), MCSpaceTwice.cfg (the     *)
(* reader keeps each copy, so a boid is in the result two times) and       *)
(* MCSpaceLeak.cfg (the space removes only the copy of the row, so the     *)
(* old copy of a boid that stopped in the middle of a write stays).        *)
(*                                                                         *)
(* The obstacles. MCSpaceObstacles.cfg checks the obstacles as the         *)
(* library writes and reads them, with one writer that moves two           *)
(* obstacles, two times in all. MCSpaceObstaclesLong.cfg has one writer    *)
(* that moves an obstacle three times. The fault models must fail:         *)
(* MCSpaceTwoWriters.cfg (two processes write the obstacles, so the index  *)
(* loses the cell of an obstacle) and MCSpaceNoCheck.cfg (the reader does  *)
(* not check the version, so it does not find an obstacle that moves       *)
(* during the read).                                                       *)
(***************************************************************************)
EXTENDS Space, TLC
====
